e":"Merge pull request #45 from Unknownflow/add-user-stories","messageBody":"Add user stories to DG","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"fd4416400e53ad1b3fd223bc3c0b3cb53efaefaf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add initial member use cases to Developer Guide","messageBody":"The Developer Guide still has an AddressBook delete-person use case\nand does not describe member addition or lookup. This leaves the\nsecretary\u0027s basic interactions with NUSocietyDesk unclear.\n\nDescribe member deletion, addition, and name-based lookup as textual\nuse cases. Keep their extensions aligned with AB3 behavior so the\nrequirements can evolve alongside the product.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":56,"deletions":11}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"687dc224f0e5036c11b40a51318329ba25ea779e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update Performance NFR","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"6d8a8774d757e63d4379dd27cab5f888a035aaa7","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #52 from hongyuuuu/normalize-tag-identity","messageBody":"Normalize tag identity","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"27369b38fa8bdf24bb80619b22d92ad7ad16a7a3","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Support explicit name searches","messageBody":"Find accepts only unprefixed name keywords. Explicit field selection\nprovides consistent syntax for phone and email searches to build on.\n\nAccept an optional n/ prefix while preserving existing name matching.\nReject empty values, repeated prefixes, and text before a prefix.\nAllow person predicates so later fields can reuse the same command.\n\nRefs #54\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":29,"deletions":11},"test-code":{"insertions":61,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"99bf62735d14b12daabb2bf39f43a155546d727e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add phone number searches","messageBody":"Find searches names only, so secretaries cannot locate members using\na remembered phone number.\n\nSupport p/ substring searches, including short digit sequences.\nReject empty values, repeated prefixes, and combined name and phone\nsearches. Preserve existing name searches and reuse the results view.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":71,"deletions":9},"test-code":{"insertions":136,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"90d912ef1dcc22211dfbef0bcb89b14f0e98e7f5","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reject multiple phone search substrings","messageBody":"Phone searches treat multiple fragments as one substring and return no\nmatches. This can make unsupported input look like a valid search.\n\nReject phone values containing whitespace-separated fragments and show\nan explanatory error. Add parser coverage for spaces, tabs, and line\nbreaks to keep the single-substring rule consistent.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":8,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":17,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"3103b4e68c8af65ea1596717f8fcfadb03f1e1bc","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document name and phone searches","messageBody":"The guides describe name searches only, leaving the new n/ and p/\nsyntax and phone search restrictions unexplained.\n\nDocument search formats, matching rules, invalid inputs, and examples\nin the User Guide. Extend UC03 with both search fields, result counts,\nand error flows so both guides match the implemented behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":54,"deletions":12}}}]}],"hongyuuuu":[{"date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"d59ffbe78b68d0bb248669ddf257b3311fc90372","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update AboutUs page for hongyuuuu","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":4,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"2dd938ca3a2696335091f9c09b41f26c46517c26","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #2